The only item that must be present in an Ascension Kit (TM) is a ring of 
free action. This is because free action is highly desirable, and wearing a 
ring is the only way to get it.

Other than that, it is a set of characteristics that your character should 
be or have (and be unable to lose very simply) or have done before 
attempting the final stage of ascension. Off the top of my head and in 
general:

- Level 14 or higher (preferably higher for spellcasters)
- Several hundred hit points
- A highly enchanted weapon the wielder is proficient in, usually an 
artifact
- A viable method of ranged attack (missile weapon, spell with sufficient 
mana or generous supply of wand charges)
- A low AC (say -35 or less) that cannot be raised too high by armour 
erosion
- Magic Cancellation 2 or 3 (some think 3 is essential but YAAPs 
demonstrate otherwise)
- The following intrinsics/extrinsics:
    Resist fire, cold, sleep, shock and poison
    Reflection
    Magic Resistance
    Very fast
    See invisible
    Protection (contributes to AC - usually at least 9 levels)
    Telepathy
- Controllable levitation
- Methods to prevent death by sliming, stoning, and drowning
- A defence from possible mind flayer attacks
- Methods of escape from crowds of hostile monsters, including on 
undiggable no teleport levels.
- At least one method of remote detection of monsters while unblinded; e.g. 
warning, extrinsic telepathy, astral vision.

I've no doubt I've missed something there. Things that some may regard as 
essential, but are not nearly as necessary IMO include:

- Teleportitis with Teleport Control (walking is always viable as an 
alternative.)
- Teleport Control or the Eye of the Aethiopica (level teleport is a useful 
escape means from a no teleport level; TC or the Eye helps guarantee you 
leave the level. But there are alternative strategies you could employ with 
crowds of monsters)
- Resist disintegration (only two possible sources of disintegration 
attacks - reflection is sufficient for one and the other can easily be 
avoided in normal play)
- Method of inducing conflict (There aren't really any situations where 
conflict is your only choice - it is highly useful though).
- Life Saving (A character with an AK is really only susceptible to death 
by stupidity - avoiding doing stupid things is a viable alternative.)
- Permanent light source - i.e. a magic lamp or astral vision (it's easy 
enough to make do without or manage ordinary light sources)
- Warning or astral vision. (extrinsic telepathy suffices as most dangerous 
monsters have a mind. Green slimes are mindless but not incredibly 
dangerous as sliming can be cured)


